(function(E){ const x = E["exam-11"] = E["exam-11"] || {units:{}}; (x.units = x.units || {})["x11-r3"] = {"id":"x11-r3","patterns":["RA-mind","GT3-life","PARA-research","PARA-cause","TR-paraphrase","TR-samewords","TR-hedge","TR-whosevoice","TR-NGvsF","TR-limit"],"title":{"en":"Reading 3: Passage 3 / Section 3","tr":"Reading 3: Passage 3 / Section 3","fa":"Reading ۳: متن ۳ (Passage 3) / بخش ۳ (Section 3)"},"objective":{"en":"After this lesson, you can follow a writer who defends an unpopular idea: answer multiple choice questions on the evidence, match sentence endings by grammar and meaning, and decide YES, NO or NOT GIVEN on the writer’s views.","tr":"Bu dersin sonunda popüler olmayan bir fikri savunan bir yazarı takip edebileceksin: Kanıtlarla ilgili çoktan seçmeli soruları cevaplayabilecek, cümle sonlarını dilbilgisine ve anlama göre eşleştirebilecek ve yazarın görüşleri için YES, NO ya da NOT GIVEN’a karar verebileceksin.","fa":"بعد از این درس می‌توانی نویسنده‌ای را که از یک ایده‌ی نامحبوب دفاع می‌کند دنبال کنی: به سؤال‌های چندگزینه‌ای درباره‌ی شواهد جواب بدهی، پایان جمله‌ها را از روی دستور و معنی جور کنی و درباره‌ی نظرهای نویسنده بین ⁨YES⁩، ⁨NO⁩ و ⁨NOT GIVEN⁩ تصمیم بگیری."},"objectiveGT":{"en":"After this lesson, you can complete a summary with one word from the text, match statements to seven people quoted in a long article, and answer multiple choice questions, including one on the writer’s purpose.","tr":"Bu dersin sonunda bir özeti metinden tek kelimeyle tamamlayabilecek, uzun bir makalede sözleri aktarılan yedi kişiyle ifadeleri eşleştirebilecek ve biri yazarın amacıyla ilgili olmak üzere çoktan seçmeli soruları cevaplayabileceksin.","fa":"بعد از این درس می‌توانی خلاصه را با یک کلمه از متن کامل کنی، جمله‌ها را با هفت نفری که در یک مقاله‌ی بلند حرفشان نقل شده جور کنی و به سؤال‌های چندگزینه‌ای، از جمله یکی درباره‌ی هدف نویسنده، جواب بدهی."},"sessions":[["explain"],["drill"],["exit"]],"explain":{"title":{"en":"Reading Passage 3: an argument about the mind","tr":"Reading Passage 3: zihin üzerine bir tartışma yazısı","fa":"Reading Passage 3: استدلالی درباره‌ی ذهن"},"objective":{"en":"After this lesson, you can follow a writer who defends an unpopular idea: answer multiple choice questions on the evidence, match sentence endings by grammar and meaning, and decide YES, NO or NOT GIVEN on the writer’s views.","tr":"Bu dersin sonunda popüler olmayan bir fikri savunan bir yazarı takip edebileceksin: Kanıtlarla ilgili çoktan seçmeli soruları cevaplayabilecek, cümle sonlarını dilbilgisine ve anlama göre eşleştirebilecek ve yazarın görüşleri için YES, NO ya da NOT GIVEN’a karar verebileceksin.","fa":"بعد از این درس می‌توانی نویسنده‌ای را که از یک ایده‌ی نامحبوب دفاع می‌کند دنبال کنی: به سؤال‌های چندگزینه‌ای درباره‌ی شواهد جواب بدهی، پایان جمله‌ها را از روی دستور و معنی جور کنی و درباره‌ی نظرهای نویسنده بین ⁨YES⁩، ⁨NO⁩ و ⁨NOT GIVEN⁩ تصمیم بگیری."},"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Questions","tr":"Soru","fa":"سؤال"},"value":"14"},{"label":{"en":"Endings","tr":"Cümle sonu","fa":"پایان جمله"},"value":"A-G"},{"label":{"en":"Time","tr":"Süre","fa":"زمان"},"value":{"en":"20 min","tr":"20 dk","fa":"۲۰ دقیقه"}}],"context":{"eyebrow":{"en":"1 The context","tr":"1 Bağlam","fa":"۱ زمینه"},"head":{"en":"This exam: the value of boredom","tr":"Bu sınav: can sıkıntısının değeri","fa":"این آزمون: ارزشِ حوصله‌سررفتن"},"intro":{"en":"Psychology and the mind are among the most frequent Academic topics, and Passage 3 often defends an idea most people reject. Follow how the writer uses evidence and where the writer limits the claim: the YES/NO answers depend on both.","tr":"Psikoloji ve zihin en sık çıkan Academic konular arasındadır ve Passage 3 çoğu zaman insanların çoğunun reddettiği bir fikri savunur. Yazarın kanıtları nasıl kullandığını ve iddiasını nerede sınırladığını takip et: YES/NO cevapları ikisine de bağlıdır.","fa":"روان‌شناسی و ذهن از پرتکرارترین موضوع‌های ⁨Academic⁩ هستند و ⁨Passage 3⁩ اغلب از ایده‌ای دفاع می‌کند که بیشتر آدم‌ها قبولش ندارند. دنبال کن نویسنده چطور از شواهد استفاده می‌کند و کجا ادعایش را محدود می‌کند: جواب‌های ⁨YES/NO⁩ به هر دو بستگی دارند."},"technique":{"en":"2 The technique","tr":"2 Teknik","fa":"۲ تکنیک"},"labels":{"asks":{"en":"What this part is about","tr":"Bu kısım ne hakkında","fa":"این بخش درباره‌ی چیست"},"fields":{"en":"Headings you will see","tr":"Göreceğin başlıklar","fa":"عنوان‌هایی که می‌بینی"},"words":{"en":"Words that carry the answers","tr":"Cevabı taşıyan kelimeler","fa":"کلمه‌هایی که جواب در آن‌هاست"},"a":{"en":"On the paper","tr":"Kâğıtta","fa":"روی برگه"},"b":{"en":"What you hear or read","tr":"Duyduğun ya da okuduğun","fa":"چیزی که می‌شنوی یا می‌خوانی"},"traps":{"en":"Traps","tr":"Tuzaklar","fa":"دام‌ها"},"example":{"en":"Example","tr":"Örnek","fa":"نمونه"},"ideas":{"en":"Ideas","tr":"Fikirler","fa":"ایده‌ها"}},"cards":[{"id":"x11-r3-ctx","exam":true,"patterns":["RA-mind","PARA-research","PARA-cause"],"often":{"pattern":"RA-mind","n":30,"of":120,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 30 of the last 120 passages","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 120 metnin 30’unda","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۳۰ متن از ۱۲۰ متنِ اخیر"}},"title":{"en":"An argument for an unpopular feeling","tr":"Sevilmeyen bir duygu için bir savunma","fa":"دفاع از احساسی که کسی دوستش ندارد"},"asks":{"en":"The writer argues that boredom has value. The passage defines it, reports experiments on creativity, questions how far they go, looks at phones and children, admits when boredom does harm and ends with a modest proposal. Multiple choice and sentence endings test the evidence; YES/NO/NOT GIVEN tests the writer's views.","tr":"Yazar can sıkıntısının bir değeri olduğunu savunuyor. Metin onu tanımlıyor, yaratıcılık üzerine deneyleri aktarıyor, bunların ne kadar ileri gidebileceğini sorguluyor, telefonlara ve çocuklara bakıyor, can sıkıntısının zarar verdiği durumları kabul ediyor ve mütevazı bir öneriyle bitiyor. Çoktan seçmeli sorular ve cümle sonları kanıtları, YES/NO/NOT GIVEN ise yazarın görüşlerini ölçer.","fa":"نویسنده استدلال می‌کند که حوصله‌سررفتن ارزش دارد. متن آن را تعریف می‌کند، آزمایش‌هایی درباره‌ی خلاقیت را گزارش می‌دهد، می‌پرسد این آزمایش‌ها تا کجا اعتبار دارند، سراغ گوشی‌ها و بچه‌ها می‌رود، می‌پذیرد که حوصله‌سررفتن کجا آسیب می‌زند و با پیشنهادی فروتنانه تمام می‌شود. چندگزینه‌ای‌ها و پایان جمله‌ها شواهد را می‌سنجند و ⁨YES/NO/NOT GIVEN⁩ نظرهای نویسنده را."},"fields":["The usual view","What boredom is","Creativity experiments","How far the research goes","Phones and pauses","Children","When boredom harms","The writer's proposal"],"words":[{"a":"end easily","b":"the solution is in your pocket","tr":"kolayca bitirmek","fa":"راحت تمام کردن"},{"a":"a signal","b":"tells us that something is not meeting our needs","tr":"bir işaret","fa":"یک نشانه"},{"a":"the dullest","b":"an even duller activity","tr":"en sıkıcı","fa":"کسل‌کننده‌ترین"},{"a":"find a solution","b":"solve it afterwards","tr":"bir çözüm bulmak","fa":"راه‌حل پیدا کردن"},{"a":"with some caution","b":"should not be exaggerated","tr":"biraz temkinle","fa":"با کمی احتیاط"},{"a":"a small amount of pain","b":"a mild electric shock","tr":"biraz acı","fa":"کمی درد"},{"a":"unplanned time","b":"nothing planned / unstructured time","tr":"plansız zaman","fa":"وقت بی‌برنامه"},{"a":"entertain themselves","b":"find something to do on their own","tr":"kendi kendini oyalamak","fa":"خودشان را سرگرم کردن"},{"a":"feeling low","b":"low mood","tr":"moralsiz hissetmek","fa":"دل‌گرفته بودن"},{"a":"short-lived","b":"occasional / the empty quarter of an hour","tr":"kısa süreli","fa":"کوتاه‌مدت"},{"a":"on purpose","b":"deliberately / designed to be","tr":"kasten","fa":"عمداً"},{"a":"worth trying","b":"small changes that cost nothing","tr":"denemeye değer","fa":"ارزش امتحان کردن دارد"}],"traps":[{"en":"The writer criticises the research (\"should not be exaggerated\") but still uses it. An option that calls it useless goes further than the writer does.","tr":"Yazar araştırmayı eleştiriyor (\"abartılmamalı\") ama yine de kullanıyor. Onu işe yaramaz diye niteleyen bir seçenek yazardan daha ileri gider.","fa":"نویسنده پژوهش را نقد می‌کند («نباید در آن اغراق کرد»)، اما باز هم از آن استفاده می‌کند. گزینه‌ای که آن را بی‌فایده بداند از خود نویسنده جلوتر می‌رود."},{"en":"\"None of this is to say...\" limits the argument. A statement that boredom is always good is NO.","tr":"\"Bunların hiçbiri ... demek değildir\" argümanı sınırlar. Can sıkıntısının her zaman iyi olduğunu söyleyen bir ifade NO’dur.","fa":"«هیچ‌کدام از این‌ها به این معنی نیست که...» استدلال را محدود می‌کند. جمله‌ای که بگوید حوصله‌سررفتن همیشه خوب است ⁨NO⁩ است."},{"en":"\"I know of no way to find out\" means the writer gives no view: NOT GIVEN, not NO.","tr":"\"Bunu öğrenmenin bir yolunu bilmiyorum\", yazarın görüş bildirmediği anlamına gelir: NO değil, NOT GIVEN.","fa":"«هیچ راهی برای فهمیدنش سراغ ندارم» یعنی نویسنده نظری نمی‌دهد: ⁨NOT GIVEN⁩، نه ⁨NO⁩."}],"example":{"text":"\"It is often claimed that boredom makes people lazy. In my view, it does the opposite: it pushes them to find something better to do.\"","item":"Statement: Boredom makes people lazy.  (views of the writer)","answer":"NO","why":{"en":"\"It is often claimed\" reports other people; \"in my view, it does the opposite\" is the writer: NO.","tr":"\"Sık sık iddia edilir\" başkalarını aktarıyor; \"bence tam tersini yapar\" yazarın görüşü: NO.","fa":"«اغلب ادعا می‌شود» حرف دیگران است؛ «به نظر من برعکس است» نظر نویسنده است: ⁨NO⁩."}}},{"id":"RA-mind-arg","ctx":["RA-mind"],"title":{"en":"Arguments about learning and society","tr":"Öğrenme ve toplum üzerine tartışma yazıları","fa":"نوشته‌های استدلالی درباره‌ی یادگیری و جامعه"},"asks":{"en":"An argument about education, behaviour or society: should children learn handwriting, does praise help, can wisdom be learned. The writer reports other views and gives their own; multiple choice and summaries follow the argument.","tr":"Eğitim, davranış ya da toplum üzerine bir tartışma yazısı: çocuklar el yazısı öğrenmeli mi, övgü işe yarar mı, bilgelik öğrenilebilir mi. Yazar başka görüşleri aktarır ve kendi görüşünü verir; çoktan seçmeli sorular ve özetler tartışmanın akışını izler.","fa":"نوشته‌ای استدلالی درباره‌ی آموزش، رفتار یا جامعه: آیا بچه‌ها باید دست‌خط یاد بگیرند، آیا تعریف کردن کمک می‌کند، آیا خرد یادگرفتنی است. نویسنده نظرهای دیگران را نقل می‌کند و نظر خودش را می‌دهد؛ چندگزینه‌ای و خلاصه‌ها مسیر استدلال را دنبال می‌کنند."},"fields":["The writer agrees with the government’s view. (YES / NO / NOT GIVEN)","What does the writer say about earlier research?","The writer’s purpose in the final paragraph is to...","Summary: many teachers ___ the importance of..."],"words":[{"a":"in favour of","b":"supports / argues for","tr":"lehinde","fa":"موافقِ"},{"a":"against","b":"opposes / objects to","tr":"aleyhinde","fa":"مخالفِ"},{"a":"misguided","b":"wrong / based on a mistake","tr":"yanlış temelli","fa":"نادرست"},{"a":"reasonable","b":"fair / makes sense","tr":"makul","fa":"منطقی"},{"a":"exaggerate","b":"overstate / make it sound bigger","tr":"abartmak","fa":"اغراق کردن"},{"a":"widely held","b":"many people believe","tr":"yaygın","fa":"رایج"},{"a":"it remains to be seen","b":"we do not know yet","tr":"henüz belli değil","fa":"هنوز معلوم نیست"},{"a":"evidence suggests","b":"research indicates","tr":"kanıtlar gösteriyor ki","fa":"شواهد نشان می‌دهد"},{"a":"sceptical","b":"doubtful","tr":"şüpheci","fa":"تردیدآمیز"},{"a":"a balanced view","b":"both sides","tr":"dengeli bir bakış","fa":"دیدگاه متعادل"},{"a":"ultimately","b":"in the end","tr":"sonuç olarak","fa":"در نهایت"},{"a":"rightly","b":"correctly / with good reason","tr":"haklı olarak","fa":"به‌درستی"}],"traps":[{"en":"The writer’s opinion often sits in one word: \"rightly\", \"wrongly\", \"surprisingly\". Watch the adverbs.","tr":"Yazarın görüşü çoğu zaman tek bir kelimededir: \"rightly\", \"wrongly\", \"surprisingly\". Zarflara dikkat et.","fa":"نظر نویسنده اغلب در یک کلمه است: «rightly»، «wrongly»، «surprisingly». به قیدها دقت کن."},{"en":"Summary with a box: the words in the box are paraphrases. Choose by meaning and by grammar.","tr":"Kutulu özet: kutudaki kelimeler başka ifadelerdir. Hem anlama hem dilbilgisine göre seç.","fa":"خلاصه با کادر: کلمه‌های کادر هم‌معنی‌اند. هم بر اساس معنی و هم بر اساس دستور انتخاب کن."}],"example":{"text":"Praising children for being clever is widely recommended. I believe this advice is misguided: children praised for their intelligence often avoid difficult tasks, in case they fail.","item":"Statement: The writer agrees that children should be praised for being clever.  (YES / NO / NOT GIVEN)","answer":"NO","why":{"en":"The advice is \"widely recommended\", but the writer calls it \"misguided\": NO.","tr":"Tavsiye \"yaygın olarak öneriliyor\" ama yazar ona \"yanlış\" diyor: NO.","fa":"این توصیه «رایج است»، ولی نویسنده آن را «نادرست» می‌داند: NO."}},"track":"academic","general":true,"patterns":["RA-mind"],"often":{"pattern":"RA-mind","n":30,"of":120,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 30 of the last 120 passages","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 120 metnin 30’unda","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۳۰ متن از ۱۲۰ متنِ اخیر"}}}]},"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"In the exam","tr":"Sınavda","fa":"در آزمون"},"head":{"en":"Choices, sentence endings, the writer's views","tr":"Seçimler, cümle sonları, yazarın görüşleri","fa":"گزینه‌ها، پایان جمله‌ها، نظرهای نویسنده"},"body":{"en":"Questions 27-30: choose A, B, C or D. Questions 31-35: complete each sentence with the correct ending, A-G; two endings are not used. Questions 36-40: YES, NO or NOT GIVEN on the writer's views.","tr":"Soru 27-30: A, B, C ya da D’yi seç. Soru 31-35: Her cümleyi doğru sonla (A-G) tamamla; iki son kullanılmaz. Soru 36-40: yazarın görüşleri için YES, NO ya da NOT GIVEN.","fa":"سؤال‌های ۲۷ تا ۳۰: ⁨A⁩، ⁨B⁩، ⁨C⁩ یا ⁨D⁩ را انتخاب کن. سؤال‌های ۳۱ تا ۳۵: هر جمله را با پایان درست (⁨A⁩ تا ⁨G⁩) کامل کن؛ دو پایان استفاده نمی‌شوند. سؤال‌های ۳۶ تا ۴۰: ⁨YES⁩، ⁨NO⁩ یا ⁨NOT GIVEN⁩ درباره‌ی نظرهای نویسنده."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The method","tr":"Yöntem","fa":"روش"},"head":{"en":"Four steps","tr":"Dört adım","fa":"چهار قدم"},"steps":[{"en":"Read the first and last paragraphs first: they give you the writer's position and its limits.","tr":"Önce ilk ve son paragrafları oku: Yazarın tutumunu ve bu tutumun sınırlarını verirler.","fa":"اول پاراگراف اول و آخر را بخوان: موضع نویسنده و حد و مرزش را نشان می‌دهند."},{"en":"For multiple choice, find the paragraph and reject options that are too strong or not stated.","tr":"Çoktan seçmeli sorularda paragrafı bul; fazla güçlü ya da metinde olmayan seçenekleri ele.","fa":"برای چندگزینه‌ای پاراگراف را پیدا کن و گزینه‌هایی را که زیادی تندند یا در متن نیامده‌اند کنار بگذار."},{"en":"For sentence endings, first rule out endings that do not fit the grammar of the beginning, then check the meaning.","tr":"Cümle sonlarında önce cümlenin başlangıcının dilbilgisine uymayan sonları ele, sonra anlamı kontrol et.","fa":"برای پایان جمله‌ها اول پایان‌هایی را که با دستور ابتدای جمله جور نیستند حذف کن و بعد معنی را بسنج."},{"en":"For YES/NO/NOT GIVEN, separate the views the writer reports from the writer's own voice: I want to argue, to me, I know of no...","tr":"YES/NO/NOT GIVEN için yazarın aktardığı görüşleri kendi sesinden ayır: I want to argue, to me, I know of no...","fa":"برای ⁨YES/NO/NOT GIVEN⁩ نظرهایی را که نویسنده نقل می‌کند از صدای خود نویسنده جدا کن: ⁨I want to argue⁩، ⁨to me⁩، ⁨I know of no⁩..."}],"wrong":"A student who studies late at night are more likely to sleep badly.","right":"A student who studies late at night is more likely to sleep badly.","tip":{"en":"Why it works: grammar removes some endings before you read for meaning. A singular beginning (a student, someone) needs a singular verb (is, has); a plural one (people, children) needs are or have. In Turkish and Persian a plural subject can take a singular verb, so this clue is easy to miss.","tr":"Neden işe yarar: Dilbilgisi, anlama bakmadan önce bazı sonları eler. Tekil bir başlangıç (a student, someone) tekil fiil (is, has), çoğul bir başlangıç (people, children) are ya da have ister. Türkçede çoğul özne tekil fiille kullanılabildiği için (\"Öğrenciler geldi\") bu ipucunu kaçırmak kolaydır.","fa":"این روش به کارت می‌آید، چون دستور زبان قبل از اینکه سراغ معنی بروی بعضی پایان‌ها را حذف می‌کند. ابتدای مفرد (⁨a student⁩، ⁨someone⁩) فعل مفرد می‌خواهد (⁨is⁩، ⁨has⁩) و ابتدای جمع (⁨people⁩، ⁨children⁩) فعل ⁨are⁩ یا ⁨have⁩. در فارسی فاعل جمعِ غیرانسان گاهی فعل مفرد می‌گیرد («کتاب‌ها روی میز است»)، برای همین این سرنخ راحت از چشم می‌افتد."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The trap","tr":"Tuzak","fa":"دام"},"head":{"en":"Too strong, not stated, just right","tr":"Fazla güçlü, söylenmemiş, tam yerinde","fa":"زیادی تند، گفته‌نشده، درست"},"table":{"headers":{"en":["The writer says","The option says","Match?"],"tr":["Yazar diyor ki","Seçenek diyor ki","Uyuyor mu?"],"fa":["نویسنده می‌گوید","گزینه می‌گوید","جور است؟"]},"rows":[["the study has some weaknesses","the study is worthless","no: too strong"],["the change may help a little","the change has a small benefit","yes"],["I cannot say whether it works","the writer believes it works","no: the writer gives no view"]]}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"One sentence ending, step by step","tr":"Bir cümle sonu, adım adım","fa":"یک پایان جمله، قدم به قدم"},"instruction":"Complete the sentence with the correct ending, A, B or C.","text":"\"Commuters who read on the train arrive at work in a better mood than those who check their emails.\"","item":"A commuter who checks emails on the train...   A are less relaxed at work.   B is likely to arrive in a worse mood.   C arrive in a better mood.","answer":"B","walk":[{"en":"The beginning is singular: \"A commuter... checks\".","tr":"Başlangıç tekil: \"A commuter... checks\".","fa":"ابتدای جمله مفرد است: «⁨A commuter... checks⁩»."},{"en":"A and C use plural verbs (are, arrive), so they cannot follow it.","tr":"A ve C çoğul fiil kullanıyor (are, arrive); bu yüzden bu başlangıca uymazlar.","fa":"⁨A⁩ و ⁨C⁩ فعل جمع دارند (⁨are⁩، ⁨arrive⁩)، پس با این ابتدا جور نیستند."},{"en":"B is singular and matches the meaning: a worse mood than readers. B.","tr":"B tekil ve anlamla da uyuşuyor: okuyanlardan daha kötü bir ruh hâli. B.","fa":"⁨B⁩ مفرد است و با معنی هم جور است: حالِ بدتر از کسانی که کتاب می‌خوانند. ⁨B⁩."}]},"quick":{"prompt":"Writer: \"Daydreaming is often dismissed as laziness. I see it differently: it is how the mind tidies up.\" Statement: \"Daydreaming is a form of laziness.\"","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"\"Often dismissed as laziness\" is other people's view; \"I see it differently\" is the writer's: NO.","tr":"\"Sık sık tembellik diye geçiştirilir\" başkalarının görüşü; \"ben farklı görüyorum\" yazarın görüşü: NO.","fa":"«اغلب تنبلی حساب می‌شود» نظر دیگران است؛ «من جور دیگری می‌بینمش» نظر نویسنده است: ⁨NO⁩."}},"remember":{"en":"Check the grammar of each sentence beginning before its meaning, and keep the writer's own voice apart from the views the writer reports. Result: you can now match sentence endings quickly and judge how far a writer's view goes.","tr":"Her cümle başlangıcında önce dilbilgisine, sonra anlama bak; yazarın kendi sesini aktardığı görüşlerden ayrı tut. Sonuç: Artık cümle sonlarını hızla eşleştirebilir, bir yazarın görüşünün ne kadar ileri gittiğini değerlendirebilirsin.","fa":"در هر ابتدای جمله اول دستور و بعد معنی را بسنج و صدای خود نویسنده را از نظرهایی که نقل می‌کند جدا نگه دار. نتیجه: حالا می‌توانی پایان جمله‌ها را سریع جور کنی و بسنجی نظر نویسنده تا کجا پیش می‌رود."},"hook":{"en":"This Passage 3 defends an unpopular feeling and then limits its own claim. The main idea: find where the writer speaks and how far the writer goes, because every YES or NO depends on it.","tr":"Bu Passage 3 sevilmeyen bir duyguyu savunur, sonra kendi iddiasını sınırlar. Ana fikir: Yazarın nerede kendi adına konuştuğunu ve ne kadar ileri gittiğini bul, çünkü her YES ya da NO buna bağlıdır.","fa":"این ⁨Passage 3⁩ از احساسی دفاع می‌کند که کسی دوستش ندارد و بعد ادعای خودش را محدود می‌کند. پیدا کن نویسنده کجا حرف خودش را می‌زند و تا کجا پیش می‌رود، چون هر ⁨YES⁩ یا ⁨NO⁩ به همین بستگی دارد."},"type":"explain","id":"c-x11-r3-e","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-11","unit":"x11-r3"},"drill":{"type":"drill","skill":"reading","part":"Academic Reading Passage 3","title":{"en":"In defence of boredom","tr":"Can sıkıntısının savunması","fa":"در دفاع از حوصله‌سررفتن"},"timed":20,"ctx":["RA-mind"],"intro":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 27-40, which are based on Reading Passage 3 below.","passage":"In defence of boredom\n\nFew feelings have a worse reputation than boredom. It is the complaint of children on long car journeys and of office workers in endless meetings, and it is usually treated as a problem to be solved as quickly as possible. For most people today, the solution is rarely further away than their pocket. Yet a growing body of research suggests that boredom, unpleasant as it is, may serve a purpose, and that in our eagerness to escape it we may be losing something of value. I want to argue that we should learn to tolerate boredom, not because it is pleasant, but because of what it can lead to.\n\nPsychologists describe boredom as the uncomfortable state of wanting to be engaged in something satisfying while being unable to find it. It is not the same as relaxation: a person lying on a beach with nothing to do may be perfectly content. Boredom, by contrast, is restless, and it makes time drag. Some researchers now regard it as a signal, rather like hunger or pain, which tells us that our present situation is not meeting our needs and pushes us to look for something better. Seen in this way, boredom is less a weakness of character than a source of motivation. A person who never felt bored, if such a person exists, would have little reason to change anything about the way they spend their time.\n\nThe most widely reported evidence concerns creativity. In one British study, volunteers who had first spent a quarter of an hour copying numbers out of a telephone directory were then asked to think of as many uses as possible for a pair of plastic cups. They produced more ideas, and more original ones, than a group who had gone straight to the task. In a follow-up experiment, volunteers who had merely read the numbers, an even duller activity, did better still. The researchers suggested that boredom allows the mind to wander, and that a wandering mind makes connections it would not make when it is focused. Other studies have found that people who take a break from a difficult problem to do an undemanding task are more likely to solve it afterwards than people who keep working on it or who rest completely.\n\nThese findings should not be exaggerated. The experiments were small, the tasks were artificial, and thinking of uses for plastic cups is a long way from writing a novel or designing a bridge. Nor does every bored mind wander somewhere useful; it may simply return to the same worries, again and again. Even so, the results fit what many writers and scientists have reported for centuries: that their best ideas tended to arrive not at the desk but in the bath, on a walk or during a dull journey.\n\nWhat has changed is how rarely we now allow ourselves such moments. Until recently, waiting for a bus or standing in a queue was an unavoidable pause in the day, a few minutes in which the mind had nothing to do but drift. Today those minutes are almost always filled. Surveys in several countries suggest that many adults pick up their phones dozens of times a day, often within seconds of any pause. In one American experiment, many of the people left alone in an empty room for fifteen minutes chose to give themselves a mild electric shock rather than simply sit with their own thoughts. The study is sometimes quoted as proof that smartphones have made us unable to cope with our own company, but that seems to me unfair. The participants had been asked to leave their phones outside, and the experiment tells us nothing about whether people were more patient before smartphones existed. I know of no reliable way to find out.\n\nThe concern is greatest for children. Many parents, anxious that their children should not waste time, fill their days with organised activities and offer them a screen whenever a gap appears. Several teachers I have spoken to report that some pupils now struggle to entertain themselves for even a few minutes without a device. One described how her class complained loudly when tablets were removed from wet break times, and then, within a fortnight, invented a complicated game of their own. It is often in unplanned time that children build things or develop interests of their own. A child who is never allowed to be bored is never forced to discover what they might do about it.\n\nNone of this is to say that boredom is always good. People who feel bored for much of the time, at work or at home, are more likely to suffer from low mood, and boredom has been linked to risky behaviour such as overeating and dangerous driving. Someone who spends eight hours a day on the same repetitive task gains nothing from being told that boredom is good for the imagination. The boredom worth defending is the occasional, short-lived kind: the empty quarter of an hour, not the empty year.\n\nWhat, then, should we do? I am not suggesting that anyone should give up their phone, or that schools should plan lessons that are dull on purpose. The aim is more modest: to notice the moment of boredom before we rush to end it, and now and then to let it run its course. Leaving the phone in another room for an hour, walking without headphones or giving children an afternoon with nothing planned are small changes. They cost nothing, and they are easy to abandon if they do not help. But if the research is even partly right, they may give the mind the space it needs to produce its best ideas.","groups":[{"instruction":"Questions 27-30. Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 27-30 on your answer sheet.","qtype":"mcq","questions":[{"n":27,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"In the first paragraph, the writer suggests that people today","options":["A rarely feel bored at all.","B can usually end their boredom very easily.","C are bored more often than in the past.","D find boredom less unpleasant than before."],"correct":1,"evidence":"the solution is rarely further away than their pocket","why":{"en":"\"The solution is rarely further away than their pocket\": a phone ends boredom at once. \"Rarely\" is about the solution, not about feeling bored.","tr":"\"Çözüm nadiren ceplerinden daha uzaktadır\": Telefon can sıkıntısını hemen bitirir. \"Rarely\" can sıkıntısını değil, çözümü anlatıyor.","fa":"«راه‌حل به‌ندرت از جیبشان دورتر است»: گوشی فوراً حوصله‌سررفتن را تمام می‌کند. «⁨rarely⁩» درباره‌ی راه‌حل است، نه درباره‌ی حوصله‌سررفتن."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase","TR-samewords"]},{"n":28,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"Why does the writer compare boredom to hunger and pain?","options":["A to show that it can be dangerous","B to explain why people try to avoid it","C to show that it has physical causes","D to suggest that it tells us something needs to change"],"correct":3,"evidence":"which tells us that our present situation is not meeting our needs","why":{"en":"Like hunger or pain, boredom is a signal that \"tells us that our present situation is not meeting our needs\".","tr":"Açlık ya da acı gibi, can sıkıntısı da \"içinde bulunduğumuz durumun ihtiyaçlarımızı karşılamadığını\" söyleyen bir işarettir.","fa":"حوصله‌سررفتن هم مثل گرسنگی یا درد نشانه‌ای است که «به ما می‌گوید وضعیت فعلی‌مان نیازهایمان را برآورده نمی‌کند»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":29,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"What did the follow-up experiment in the third paragraph show?","options":["A The dullest activity was followed by the most creative results.","B Copying numbers was more boring than reading them.","C Most volunteers preferred reading to writing.","D Ideas came more quickly after a complete rest."],"correct":0,"evidence":"volunteers who had merely read the numbers, an even duller activity, did better still","why":{"en":"Reading the numbers was \"an even duller activity\", and those volunteers \"did better still\". B reverses the text.","tr":"Numaraları okumak \"daha da sıkıcı bir etkinlikti\" ve bu gönüllüler \"daha da iyi sonuç aldı\". B metni tersine çeviriyor.","fa":"خواندن عددها «کاری حتی کسل‌کننده‌تر» بود و این داوطلب‌ها «باز هم بهتر عمل کردند». گزینه‌ی ⁨B⁩ حرف متن را برعکس کرده."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":30,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"What point does the writer make about the creativity research in the fourth paragraph?","options":["A It has been repeated in many countries.","B Its methods were too poor for it to be useful.","C Its results should be treated with some caution.","D It contradicts the experience of most writers."],"correct":2,"evidence":"These findings should not be exaggerated","why":{"en":"\"These findings should not be exaggerated\": the experiments were small and artificial, but the results still \"fit\" what writers report. B goes too far.","tr":"\"Bu bulgular abartılmamalı\": Deneyler küçük ve yapay, ama sonuçlar yazarların anlattıklarıyla yine de \"örtüşüyor\". B fazla ileri gidiyor.","fa":"«نباید در این یافته‌ها اغراق کرد»: آزمایش‌ها کوچک و مصنوعی‌اند، اما نتیجه‌ها باز هم با تجربه‌ی نویسنده‌ها «جور درمی‌آیند». گزینه‌ی ⁨B⁩ زیادی تند است."},"trap":["TR-hedge","TR-paraphrase"]}]},{"instruction":"Questions 31-35. Complete each sentence with the correct ending, A-G, below. Write the correct letter, A-G, in boxes 31-35 on your answer sheet.","qtype":"sentence-endings","bank":["A are more likely to find a solution afterwards.","B may never discover how to entertain themselves.","C produce fewer ideas than people who rest completely.","D are at greater risk of feeling low.","E chose a small amount of pain over time alone with their thoughts.","F has little to gain from the argument that boredom is useful.","G check their phones less often than adults do."],"questions":[{"n":31,"kind":"match","prompt":"People who leave a hard problem to do an easy task for a while","correct":0,"evidence":"are more likely to solve it afterwards than people who keep working on it or who rest completely","why":{"en":"People who take a break to do an undemanding task \"are more likely to solve it afterwards\". C is the opposite of the finding.","tr":"Ara verip kolay bir iş yapanların \"sonradan sorunu çözme olasılığı daha yüksek\". C bulgunun tam tersi.","fa":"کسانی که وقفه می‌دهند و کار ساده‌ای می‌کنند «بیشتر احتمال دارد بعداً مسئله را حل کنند». گزینه‌ی ⁨C⁩ برعکس این یافته است."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":32,"kind":"match","prompt":"Many of the people left alone in an empty room","correct":4,"evidence":"chose to give themselves a mild electric shock rather than simply sit with their own thoughts","why":{"en":"They \"chose to give themselves a mild electric shock rather than simply sit with their own thoughts\": a mild shock = a small amount of pain.","tr":"\"Sadece kendi düşünceleriyle oturmak yerine kendilerine hafif bir elektrik şoku vermeyi seçtiler\": a mild shock = a small amount of pain.","fa":"«ترجیح دادند به خودشان شوک الکتریکی خفیفی بدهند تا اینکه فقط با فکرهای خودشان بنشینند»: ⁨a mild shock⁩ یعنی ⁨a small amount of pain⁩."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":33,"kind":"match","prompt":"Children who are never left with time to fill","correct":1,"evidence":"A child who is never allowed to be bored is never forced to discover what they might do about it","why":{"en":"\"A child who is never allowed to be bored is never forced to discover what they might do about it.\" The text does not compare children's and adults' phone use (G).","tr":"\"Sıkılmasına hiç izin verilmeyen bir çocuk, bu konuda ne yapabileceğini keşfetmek zorunda da kalmaz.\" Metin, çocuklarla yetişkinlerin telefon kullanımını karşılaştırmıyor (G).","fa":"«بچه‌ای که هیچ‌وقت اجازه ندارد حوصله‌اش سر برود، هیچ‌وقت مجبور نمی‌شود کشف کند برای آن چه کاری از دستش برمی‌آید». متن استفاده‌ی بچه‌ها و بزرگ‌ترها از گوشی را مقایسه نمی‌کند (⁨G⁩)."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase","TR-samewords"]},{"n":34,"kind":"match","prompt":"People who are bored for much of the time","correct":3,"evidence":"are more likely to suffer from low mood","why":{"en":"They \"are more likely to suffer from low mood\": at greater risk of feeling low.","tr":"\"Moral bozukluğu yaşama olasılıkları daha yüksek\": at greater risk of feeling low.","fa":"«بیشتر احتمال دارد دچار دل‌گرفتگی و روحیه‌ی پایین شوند»: یعنی ⁨at greater risk of feeling low⁩."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":35,"kind":"match","prompt":"Someone doing the same repetitive task all day","correct":5,"evidence":"gains nothing from being told that boredom is good for the imagination","why":{"en":"Such a person \"gains nothing from being told that boredom is good for the imagination\". The singular beginning also fits \"has\" in F.","tr":"Böyle biri \"can sıkıntısının hayal gücüne iyi geldiğini duymaktan hiçbir şey kazanmaz\". Tekil başlangıç da F’deki \"has\" ile uyuşuyor.","fa":"چنین کسی «از شنیدن اینکه حوصله‌سررفتن برای تخیل خوب است هیچ سودی نمی‌برد». ابتدای مفرد جمله هم با «⁨has⁩» در ⁨F⁩ جور است."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]}]},{"instruction":"Questions 36-40. Do the following statements agree with the views of the writer in Reading Passage 3? In boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement agrees with the views of the writer, NO if the statement contradicts the views of the writer, NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","qtype":"ynng","questions":[{"n":36,"kind":"ynng","prompt":"Boredom is a sign of a weak character.","correct":"NO","evidence":"boredom is less a weakness of character than a source of motivation","why":{"en":"The writer says boredom \"is less a weakness of character than a source of motivation\".","tr":"Yazar can sıkıntısının \"bir karakter zayıflığından çok bir motivasyon kaynağı\" olduğunu söylüyor.","fa":"نویسنده می‌گوید حوصله‌سررفتن «بیشتر منبع انگیزه است تا ضعف شخصیت»."},"trap":["TR-whosevoice","TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":37,"kind":"ynng","prompt":"The electric-shock experiment proves that smartphones have made people unable to be alone with their thoughts.","correct":"NO","evidence":"but that seems to me unfair","why":{"en":"The writer calls this reading of the study \"unfair\": the phones were outside the room.","tr":"Yazar çalışmanın bu şekilde yorumlanmasını \"haksız\" buluyor: Telefonlar odanın dışındaydı.","fa":"نویسنده درباره‌ی این برداشت از پژوهش می‌گوید «به نظرم بی‌انصافی است»: گوشی‌ها بیرون اتاق بودند."},"trap":["TR-whosevoice"]},{"n":38,"kind":"ynng","prompt":"People coped better with boredom before smartphones were invented.","correct":"NOT GIVEN","evidence":"I know of no reliable way to find out","why":{"en":"The writer says the experiment tells us nothing about this and \"I know of no reliable way to find out\": no view.","tr":"Yazar deneyin bu konuda bir şey söylemediğini ve \"bunu öğrenmenin güvenilir bir yolunu bilmediğini\" söylüyor: görüş yok.","fa":"نویسنده می‌گوید آزمایش در این باره چیزی نمی‌گوید و «هیچ راه مطمئنی برای فهمیدنش سراغ ندارم»: پس نظری نمی‌دهد."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF","TR-hedge"]},{"n":39,"kind":"ynng","prompt":"Boredom that lasts for long periods can be harmful.","correct":"YES","evidence":"The boredom worth defending is the occasional, short-lived kind","why":{"en":"The writer defends only \"the occasional, short-lived kind\" and links boredom for much of the time with low mood and risky behaviour.","tr":"Yazar yalnızca \"ara sıra yaşanan, kısa süreli türü\" savunuyor ve sürekli can sıkıntısını moral bozukluğu ve riskli davranışla ilişkilendiriyor.","fa":"نویسنده فقط از «نوعِ گاه‌به‌گاه و کوتاهِ» آن دفاع می‌کند و حوصله‌سررفتنِ همیشگی را با روحیه‌ی پایین و رفتارهای پرخطر مرتبط می‌داند."},"trap":["TR-whosevoice","TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":40,"kind":"ynng","prompt":"Making small changes to daily routines is worthwhile.","correct":"YES","evidence":"they may give the mind the space it needs to produce its best ideas","why":{"en":"The writer recommends small changes because \"they may give the mind the space it needs\".","tr":"Yazar küçük değişiklikler öneriyor, çünkü \"zihne ihtiyaç duyduğu alanı verebilirler\".","fa":"نویسنده تغییرهای کوچک را پیشنهاد می‌کند، چون «ممکن است فضایی را که ذهن لازم دارد به آن بدهند»."},"trap":["TR-hedge"]}]}],"id":"c-x11-r3-d","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-11","unit":"x11-r3"},"exit":{"type":"exit","items":[{"tests":"word","point":1,"prompt":"\"The boredom worth defending is the occasional, short-lived kind.\" Short-lived means...","options":["lasting only a short time","felt mainly by young people","very strong"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"Short-lived = lasting a short time.","tr":"Short-lived = kısa süren.","fa":"⁨short-lived⁩ یعنی کوتاه‌مدت."}},{"tests":"paraphrase","point":1,"prompt":"An option says \"should be treated with some caution\". Which words in a passage match it?","options":["these findings should not be exaggerated","the results fit what writers have reported","the experiments were repeated"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"Not exaggerating the findings = treating them with caution.","tr":"Bulguları abartmamak = onlara temkinle yaklaşmak.","fa":"اغراق نکردن در یافته‌ها یعنی با احتیاط با آن‌ها برخورد کردن."}},{"tests":"method","point":2,"prompt":"A sentence begins \"Someone who...\". Which ending can you rule out at once?","options":["...has little to gain from it.","...are more likely to feel low.","...may never notice it."],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"\"Someone\" is singular; \"are\" needs a plural subject.","tr":"\"Someone\" tekildir; \"are\" çoğul özne ister.","fa":"«⁨someone⁩» مفرد است؛ «⁨are⁩» فاعل جمع می‌خواهد."}},{"tests":"trap","point":3,"prompt":"Writer: \"I am not suggesting that schools should plan lessons that are dull on purpose.\" Statement: \"Schools should plan some lessons to be dull.\"","options":["YES","NOT GIVEN","NO"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"\"I am not suggesting\" rejects the idea, so the statement contradicts the writer's view.","tr":"\"Bunu önermiyorum\" fikri reddediyor; yani ifade yazarın görüşüyle çelişiyor.","fa":"«پیشنهاد نمی‌کنم» یعنی نویسنده این ایده را رد می‌کند، پس جمله با نظر او تناقض دارد."}}],"id":"c-x11-r3-x","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-11","unit":"x11-r3"},"gt":{"explain":{"title":{"en":"GT Reading Section 3: a school's experiment, many voices","tr":"GT Reading Section 3: bir okulun deneyi, birçok ses","fa":"GT Reading Section 3: آزمایش یک مدرسه، نظر چند نفر"},"objective":{"en":"After this lesson, you can complete a summary with one word from the text, match statements to seven people quoted in a long article, and answer multiple choice questions, including one on the writer’s purpose.","tr":"Bu dersin sonunda bir özeti metinden tek kelimeyle tamamlayabilecek, uzun bir makalede sözleri aktarılan yedi kişiyle ifadeleri eşleştirebilecek ve biri yazarın amacıyla ilgili olmak üzere çoktan seçmeli soruları cevaplayabileceksin.","fa":"بعد از این درس می‌توانی خلاصه را با یک کلمه از متن کامل کنی، جمله‌ها را با هفت نفری که در یک مقاله‌ی بلند حرفشان نقل شده جور کنی و به سؤال‌های چندگزینه‌ای، از جمله یکی درباره‌ی هدف نویسنده، جواب بدهی."},"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Questions","tr":"Soru","fa":"سؤال"},"value":"13"},{"label":{"en":"People","tr":"Kişi","fa":"آدم‌ها"},"value":"A-G"},{"label":{"en":"Time","tr":"Süre","fa":"زمان"},"value":{"en":"20 min","tr":"20 dk","fa":"۲۰ دقیقه"}}],"context":{"eyebrow":{"en":"1 The context","tr":"1 Bağlam","fa":"۱ زمینه"},"head":{"en":"This exam: a school that locks away phones","tr":"Bu sınav: telefonları kilit altına alan bir okul","fa":"این آزمون: مدرسه‌ای که گوشی‌ها را قفل می‌کند"},"intro":{"en":"Daily life, work and society are among the most frequent GT Section 3 topics. An article like this one reports a change through the voices of the people it affects, so matching statements to people is the central task, and the last question asks about the article as a whole.","tr":"Gündelik hayat, iş ve toplum GT Section 3’ün en sık çıkan konuları arasındadır. Bunun gibi bir makale bir değişikliği ondan etkilenen insanların sesleriyle anlatır; bu yüzden ifadeleri kişilerle eşleştirmek asıl görevdir, son soru da makalenin bütününü sorar.","fa":"زندگی روزمره، کار و جامعه از پرتکرارترین موضوع‌های ⁨GT Section 3⁩ هستند. مقاله‌ای مثل این، یک تغییر را از زبان آدم‌هایی که درگیرش هستند روایت می‌کند، پس جور کردن جمله‌ها با آدم‌ها کار اصلی است و سؤال آخر درباره‌ی کل مقاله است."},"technique":{"en":"2 The technique","tr":"2 Teknik","fa":"۲ تکنیک"},"labels":{"asks":{"en":"What this part is about","tr":"Bu kısım ne hakkında","fa":"این بخش درباره‌ی چیست"},"fields":{"en":"Headings you will see","tr":"Göreceğin başlıklar","fa":"عنوان‌هایی که می‌بینی"},"words":{"en":"Words that carry the answers","tr":"Cevabı taşıyan kelimeler","fa":"کلمه‌هایی که جواب در آن‌هاست"},"a":{"en":"On the paper","tr":"Kâğıtta","fa":"روی برگه"},"b":{"en":"What you hear or read","tr":"Duyduğun ya da okuduğun","fa":"چیزی که می‌شنوی یا می‌خوانی"},"traps":{"en":"Traps","tr":"Tuzaklar","fa":"دام‌ها"},"example":{"en":"Example","tr":"Örnek","fa":"نمونه"},"ideas":{"en":"Ideas","tr":"Fikirler","fa":"ایده‌ها"}},"cards":[{"id":"x11-r3gt-ctx","exam":true,"patterns":["GT3-life","PARA-research","PARA-cause"],"often":{"pattern":"GT3-life","n":14,"of":40,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 14 of the last 40 tests","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 40 sınavın 14’ünde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۱۴ آزمون از ۴۰ آزمونِ اخیر"}},"title":{"en":"An article on a school phone ban","tr":"Okulda telefon yasağı üzerine bir makale","fa":"مقاله‌ای درباره‌ی ممنوعیت گوشی در مدرسه"},"asks":{"en":"A newspaper-style article tells the story of one school's phone policy: how it began, how it works, why it was introduced, how students, parents and staff reacted, what has changed and what a researcher thinks. Seven people are named, and the article ends with the head teacher's own view.","tr":"Gazete üslubunda bir makale bir okulun telefon politikasını anlatıyor: nasıl başladığı, nasıl işlediği, neden getirildiği, öğrencilerin, velilerin ve personelin nasıl tepki verdiği, neyin değiştiği ve bir araştırmacının ne düşündüğü. Yedi kişinin adı geçiyor ve makale okul müdürünün kendi görüşüyle bitiyor.","fa":"مقاله‌ای به سبک روزنامه ماجرای سیاست گوشی در یک مدرسه را تعریف می‌کند: چطور شروع شد، چطور کار می‌کند، چرا آمد، دانش‌آموزها و والدین و کارکنان چه واکنشی نشان دادند، چه چیزی عوض شد و یک پژوهشگر چه فکر می‌کند. اسم هفت نفر می‌آید و مقاله با نظر خود مدیر مدرسه تمام می‌شود."},"fields":["The announcement","How the pouches work","The reason","Students","Parents","Lunchtimes","Results","Other schools"],"words":[{"a":"opposed","b":"signed a petition against","tr":"karşı çıktı","fa":"مخالفت کرد"},{"a":"paid for","b":"out of its own budget","tr":"parasını ödedi","fa":"هزینه‌اش را داد"},{"a":"make people obey","b":"enforce","tr":"uymaya zorlamak","fa":"وادار به رعایت کردن"},{"a":"outside lessons","b":"at break and lunchtime","tr":"ders dışında","fa":"بیرون از کلاس"},{"a":"extra work","b":"spent more time dealing with","tr":"ek iş","fa":"کار اضافه"},{"a":"chat more at lunch","b":"people play games and talk to each other","tr":"öğle arasında daha çok sohbet etmek","fa":"سر ناهار بیشتر گپ زدن"},{"a":"keep in touch","b":"reply to messages / contact their families","tr":"iletişimi sürdürmek","fa":"در تماس ماندن"},{"a":"better information","b":"explained more clearly at the start","tr":"daha iyi bilgilendirme","fa":"اطلاع‌رسانی بهتر"},{"a":"discover a new interest","b":"find out that they actually enjoy it","tr":"yeni bir ilgi alanı keşfetmek","fa":"علاقه‌ای تازه پیدا کردن"},{"a":"when it rains","b":"on wet days","tr":"yağmur yağınca","fa":"وقتی باران می‌آید"},{"a":"difficult to know","b":"very hard to say","tr":"bilmesi zor","fa":"سخت است بدانیم"},{"a":"long-term","b":"over several years","tr":"uzun vadeli","fa":"بلندمدت"}],"traps":[{"en":"The writer's report of a group (\"some older students complain\") is not a named person's view. Match only words that belong to one person.","tr":"Yazarın bir grubu aktarması (\"bazı büyük öğrenciler şikâyet ediyor\") adı verilen bir kişinin görüşü değildir. Yalnızca tek bir kişiye ait sözleri eşleştir.","fa":"گزارش نویسنده از یک گروه («بعضی دانش‌آموزهای بزرگ‌تر شکایت دارند») نظر یک شخص نام‌برده نیست. فقط حرف‌هایی را جور کن که مال یک نفرند."},{"en":"Two people can speak about the same topic, such as information for parents. Read what each one actually says.","tr":"İki kişi aynı konudan, örneğin velilerin bilgilendirilmesinden söz edebilir. Her birinin gerçekte ne dediğini oku.","fa":"دو نفر ممکن است درباره‌ی یک موضوع حرف بزنند، مثلاً اطلاع‌رسانی به والدین. ببین هر کدام دقیقاً چه می‌گوید."}],"example":{"text":"\"The caretaker, Bill Ross, says the new bins are emptied every day. A teacher, Ann Lee, thinks there are still too few of them.\"","item":"Who thinks more bins are needed?","answer":"Ann Lee","why":{"en":"Ross talks about how often the bins are emptied; \"still too few\" is Lee's view.","tr":"Ross çöp kutularının ne sıklıkla boşaltıldığından söz ediyor; \"hâlâ çok az\" Lee’nin görüşü.","fa":"راس از اینکه سطل‌ها چند وقت یک بار خالی می‌شوند حرف می‌زند؛ «هنوز خیلی کم‌اند» نظر لی است."}}},{"id":"GT3-life","ctx":["GT3-life"],"title":{"en":"Society, work and daily life","tr":"Toplum, iş ve gündelik yaşam","fa":"جامعه، کار و زندگی روزمره"},"asks":{"en":"A text about modern life, work or society: a nursery without toys, emojis, a health programme, lessons in leadership, life in a cold town. Headings and multiple choice test the writer’s main points.","tr":"Modern yaşam, iş ya da toplum hakkında bir metin: oyuncaksız bir kreş, emojiler, bir sağlık programı, liderlik dersleri, soğuk bir kasabada yaşam. Başlıklar ve çoktan seçmeli sorular yazarın ana noktalarını sınar.","fa":"متنی درباره‌ی زندگی امروز، کار یا جامعه: مهدکودکی بدون اسباب‌بازی، ایموجی‌ها، یک برنامه‌ی سلامت، درس‌هایی درباره‌ی رهبری، زندگی در یک شهر سرد. عنوان‌ها و سؤال‌های چندگزینه‌ای نکته‌های اصلی نویسنده را می‌سنجند."},"fields":["An experiment that surprised parents","Mixed reactions from staff","The original purpose","Plans to expand the scheme","Which paragraph describes the results after a year?"],"words":[{"a":"scheme","b":"programme / project","tr":"program, uygulama","fa":"طرح"},{"a":"reaction","b":"response / what people thought","tr":"tepki","fa":"واکنش"},{"a":"mixed","b":"some liked it, others did not","tr":"karışık","fa":"دوگانه"},{"a":"surprising","b":"unexpected / few predicted it","tr":"şaşırtıcı","fa":"غافلگیرکننده"},{"a":"purpose","b":"aim / designed to","tr":"amaç","fa":"هدف"},{"a":"expand","b":"grow / extend to more places","tr":"genişletmek","fa":"گسترش دادن"},{"a":"residents","b":"locals / people who live there","tr":"sakinler","fa":"ساکنان"},{"a":"wellbeing","b":"health and happiness","tr":"iyi oluş","fa":"سلامت و رضایت"},{"a":"communicate","b":"express / get a message across","tr":"iletişim kurmak","fa":"ارتباط برقرار کردن"},{"a":"encourage","b":"motivate / persuade","tr":"teşvik etmek","fa":"تشویق کردن"},{"a":"trend","b":"something becoming common","tr":"eğilim","fa":"روند"},{"a":"outcome","b":"result / what happened","tr":"sonuç","fa":"نتیجه"}],"traps":[{"en":"\"Mixed reactions\" needs both sides in the paragraph. One positive comment is not enough.","tr":"\"Karışık tepkiler\" için paragrafta iki taraf da olmalı. Tek bir olumlu yorum yetmez.","fa":"«واکنش‌های دوگانه» یعنی هر دو طرف در پاراگراف باشند. یک نظر مثبت کافی نیست."},{"en":"The purpose of a scheme and its result are often in different paragraphs.","tr":"Bir uygulamanın amacı ve sonucu çoğu zaman farklı paragraflardadır.","fa":"هدف یک طرح و نتیجه‌اش اغلب در پاراگراف‌های جدا هستند."}],"example":{"text":"E  Not everyone was convinced. Several parents worried that their children would be bored without toys, while a few teachers felt the experiment had started too quickly. Others, however, praised the calmer atmosphere.","item":"Choose the heading for paragraph E:  i  Mixed reactions   ii  Children become bored   iii  How the toys were chosen","answer":"i","why":{"en":"Worries from parents and teachers, then praise from others: both sides, so mixed reactions.","tr":"Ebeveyn ve öğretmenlerin endişeleri, ardından başkalarının övgüsü: iki taraf da var, yani karışık tepkiler.","fa":"نگرانی پدر و مادرها و معلم‌ها، بعد تعریف دیگران: هر دو طرف هست، پس واکنش‌های دوگانه."}},"track":"gt","general":true,"patterns":["GT3-life"],"often":{"pattern":"GT3-life","n":14,"of":40,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 14 of the last 40 tests","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 40 sınavın 14’ünde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۱۴ آزمون از ۴۰ آزمونِ اخیر"}}}]},"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"In the exam","tr":"Sınavda","fa":"در آزمون"},"head":{"en":"Summary, people, choices","tr":"Özet, kişiler, seçimler","fa":"خلاصه، آدم‌ها، گزینه‌ها"},"body":{"en":"Questions 28-30: complete a summary of the opening paragraphs with ONE WORD ONLY. Questions 31-36: match six statements to seven people, A-G; one person is not used. Questions 37-40: choose A, B, C or D; the last question asks about the purpose of the whole article.","tr":"Soru 28-30: açılış paragraflarının özetini YALNIZCA BİR KELİMEYLE tamamla. Soru 31-36: altı ifadeyi yedi kişiyle (A-G) eşleştir; bir kişi kullanılmaz. Soru 37-40: A, B, C ya da D’yi seç; son soru makalenin bütününün amacını soruyor.","fa":"سؤال‌های ۲۸ تا ۳۰: خلاصه‌ی پاراگراف‌های اول را فقط با یک کلمه کامل کن. سؤال‌های ۳۱ تا ۳۶: شش جمله را با هفت نفر (⁨A⁩ تا ⁨G⁩) جور کن؛ یک نفر استفاده نمی‌شود. سؤال‌های ۳۷ تا ۴۰: ⁨A⁩، ⁨B⁩، ⁨C⁩ یا ⁨D⁩ را انتخاب کن؛ سؤال آخر هدف کل مقاله را می‌پرسد."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The method","tr":"Yöntem","fa":"روش"},"head":{"en":"Four steps","tr":"Dört adım","fa":"چهار قدم"},"steps":[{"en":"Do the summary first: it covers only the opening paragraphs.","tr":"Önce özeti yap: Yalnızca açılış paragraflarını kapsar.","fa":"اول خلاصه را حل کن: فقط پاراگراف‌های اول را پوشش می‌دهد."},{"en":"Mark each person's name and role, and underline the words inside their quotation marks.","tr":"Her kişinin adını ve görevini işaretle, tırnak içindeki sözlerinin altını çiz.","fa":"اسم و نقش هر نفر را علامت بزن و زیر حرف‌هایی که داخل گیومه آمده خط بکش."},{"en":"Match each statement to one person's own words; a sentence about a group belongs to no one in the list.","tr":"Her ifadeyi bir kişinin kendi sözleriyle eşleştir; bir grup hakkındaki cümle listedeki kimseye ait değildir.","fa":"هر جمله را با حرف خود یک نفر جور کن؛ جمله‌ای درباره‌ی یک گروه مال هیچ‌کس در فهرست نیست."},{"en":"For the purpose question, choose the option that covers the whole article, not one paragraph.","tr":"Amaç sorusu için tek bir paragrafı değil, makalenin bütününü kapsayan seçeneği seç.","fa":"برای سؤال هدف، گزینه‌ای را انتخاب کن که کل مقاله را پوشش بدهد، نه یک پاراگراف را."}],"wrong":"Phones are locked in a ___ (ONE WORD ONLY): fabric pouch","right":"Phones are locked in a ___ (ONE WORD ONLY): pouch","tip":{"en":"Why it works: the summary repeats the opening in other words, so it is quick to do first. ONE WORD ONLY means one: \"fabric pouch\" is two words and scores nothing, even though both words are in the text. Speakers of Persian and Turkish often copy an adjective and its noun as one unit; the gap needs only the noun.","tr":"Neden işe yarar: Özet açılışı başka kelimelerle tekrarlar, bu yüzden önce yapması hızlıdır. YALNIZCA BİR KELİME gerçekten tek kelime demektir: \"fabric pouch\" iki kelimedir ve iki kelime de metinde geçse bile puan getirmez. Sıfatı ismiyle birlikte tek parça gibi kopyalamak çok sık yapılan bir hatadır; buradaki boşluk yalnızca ismi ister.","fa":"این روش به کارت می‌آید، چون خلاصه همان بخش اول را با کلمه‌های دیگر تکرار می‌کند و حل کردنش در اول کار سریع است. «فقط یک کلمه» یعنی واقعاً یک کلمه: «⁨fabric pouch⁩» دو کلمه است و نمره‌ای ندارد، حتی اگر هر دو کلمه در متن باشند. در فارسی صفت با کسره‌ی اضافه به اسم می‌چسبد («کیسه‌ی پارچه‌ای») و راحت یک واحد به نظر می‌رسد، اما این جای خالی فقط اسم را می‌خواهد."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The trap","tr":"Tuzak","fa":"دام"},"head":{"en":"Purpose: the whole article, not one part","tr":"Amaç: tek bir kısım değil, bütün makale","fa":"هدف: کل مقاله، نه یک بخش"},"table":{"headers":{"en":["If the option...","Then it is..."],"tr":["Seçenek...","O zaman..."],"fa":["اگر گزینه...","پس..."]},"rows":[["describes only one paragraph","too narrow"],["takes a side the writer does not take","too strong"],["covers the whole article and its different views","the answer"]]}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"One person, step by step","tr":"Bir kişi, adım adım","fa":"یک نفر، قدم به قدم"},"instruction":"Match each statement with the correct person.","text":"\"The café owner, Rosa Diaz, says business has grown since the market opened. A resident, Ian Holt, admits he was against the market at first, but now shops there every week.\"","item":"Statement: Someone changed their mind about the market.","answer":"Ian Holt","walk":[{"en":"The idea: a change of opinion.","tr":"Fikir: bir görüş değişikliği.","fa":"ایده: عوض شدن نظر."},{"en":"Diaz talks about business, not about changing her mind.","tr":"Diaz işlerin gidişatından söz ediyor, fikrinin değişmesinden değil.","fa":"دیاز از کاسبی حرف می‌زند، نه از عوض شدن نظرش."},{"en":"Holt \"was against the market at first, but now shops there\": Ian Holt.","tr":"Holt \"başta pazara karşıydı ama şimdi orada alışveriş yapıyor\": Ian Holt.","fa":"هولت «اولش با بازار مخالف بود، اما حالا از آن‌جا خرید می‌کند»: ⁨Ian Holt⁩."}]},"quick":{"prompt":"An article describes a new night bus, quotes passengers who like it and a driver who worries about safety, and gives the cost of the service. What is the writer’s main purpose?","options":["to persuade readers to use the bus","to report the new service and different views of it","to complain about the cost"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"The article reports facts and several views without taking a side: it reports the service and the views of it.","tr":"Makale taraf tutmadan bilgileri ve farklı görüşleri aktarıyor: Hizmeti ve onunla ilgili görüşleri anlatıyor.","fa":"مقاله بدون طرف‌داری واقعیت‌ها و چند نظر را می‌آورد: هدفش گزارش این خدمت و نظرها درباره‌ی آن است."}},"remember":{"en":"Do the summary first with one word only, mark names and roles, match each statement to one person's own words, and judge the purpose on the whole article. Result: you can now match statements to the right person and choose the purpose of a whole article.","tr":"Önce özeti yalnızca bir kelimeyle yap, isimleri ve görevleri işaretle, her ifadeyi bir kişinin kendi sözleriyle eşleştir ve amacı bütün makaleye göre belirle. Sonuç: Artık ifadeleri doğru kişiyle eşleştirebilir, bütün bir makalenin amacını seçebilirsin.","fa":"اول خلاصه را فقط با یک کلمه حل کن، اسم و نقش آدم‌ها را علامت بزن، هر جمله را با حرف خود یک نفر جور کن و هدف را بر اساس کل مقاله بسنج. نتیجه: حالا می‌توانی جمله‌ها را با آدم درست جور کنی و هدف کل یک مقاله را انتخاب کنی."},"hook":{"en":"This Section 3 reports a school's phone policy through many voices. The main idea: match each statement to one person's own words, not to the writer's report of a group.","tr":"Bu Section 3 bir okulun telefon politikasını birçok sesle anlatır. Ana fikir: Her ifadeyi yazarın bir grup hakkındaki aktarımıyla değil, bir kişinin kendi sözleriyle eşleştir.","fa":"این ⁨Section 3⁩ سیاست گوشی یک مدرسه را از زبان آدم‌های زیادی می‌گوید. هر جمله را با حرف خود یک نفر جور کن، نه با گزارش نویسنده از یک گروه."},"type":"explain","id":"c-x11-r3-e-gt","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-11","unit":"x11-r3"},"drill":{"type":"drill","skill":"reading","part":"General Training Reading Section 3","title":{"en":"The day the phones went into pouches","tr":"Telefonların keselere girdiği gün","fa":"روزی که گوشی‌ها رفتند توی کیسه"},"timed":20,"ctx":["GT3-life"],"texts":[{"title":"The day the phones went into pouches","kind":"article","body":"When Castlegate Academy, a secondary school of 1,200 students in the north of England, announced that mobile phones would be locked away for the whole school day, the reaction was immediate. Within a week, more than 500 parents had signed an online petition against the plan, and a local radio station spent an afternoon taking calls about it. Two years later, the policy is still in place, and head teachers from other schools regularly travel to see how it works.\n\nThe system itself is simple. Each morning, students place their phones in a fabric pouch that closes with a magnetic lock. They keep the pouch with them all day, but it can only be opened by tapping it on one of the unlocking points at the school gates as they leave. The pouches cost about £15 each, and the school paid for them out of its own budget rather than asking families to contribute. Before the change, phones had been allowed in school as long as they were not used in lessons, a rule that teachers found almost impossible to enforce.\n\nThe head teacher, Diane Okafor, says the decision was not mainly about lessons. \"Most of our problems with phones happened at break and lunchtime,\" she explains. \"Arguments that started online carried on in the corridors, and some students spent the whole of lunch looking at a screen without speaking to anyone.\" She admits that the first term was difficult. \"For a few weeks, staff spent more time dealing with students who refused to hand in their phones than they had ever spent on phones before.\"\n\nStudents' views are mixed. Fifteen-year-old Amira Shah was strongly against the plan at first. \"I thought it was treating us like children,\" she says. \"But lunch is louder now, in a good way. People actually play games and talk to each other.\" Not everyone agrees. Some older students complain that they can no longer reply to messages about part-time jobs or contact their families during the day. The school's answer is that phones in the main office can be used for urgent calls.\n\nFor many parents, the main worry was safety. Mark Lindqvist, whose son is in Year 8, was one of those who signed the petition. \"My concern was simple: what if something happens on the way to school and he can't call me?\" he says. \"In fact, he can, because the pouch opens at the gate. I wish the school had explained that more clearly at the start, because a lot of the anger came from people who didn't understand how it would work.\" The chair of the school's governors, Paul Hendry, points out that two public meetings were held before the policy began. \"Only about forty parents came,\" he says.\n\nStaff report changes that are harder to measure. Tom Barrett, who teaches PE, says the number of students using the sports hall at lunchtime has roughly doubled. \"Some of them come along because they're bored and there's nothing else to do,\" he says. \"Then they discover that they actually enjoy it, and they keep coming back.\" The school librarian, Grace Mensah, has seen a similar effect. \"We've had to buy more board games and chess sets,\" she says. \"On wet days, the library is now completely full.\"\n\nThe school says that reports of online bullying have fallen and that results in national exams improved slightly last summer. However, Dr Helen Carver, an education researcher who has studied phone policies in a number of schools, warns against reading too much into one school's experience. \"Exam results go up and down for all sorts of reasons,\" she says. \"Schools that introduce these policies are often making several other changes at the same time, so it is very hard to say what has made the difference.\" She would like to see a large study that follows schools with and without bans over several years.\n\nMeanwhile, Castlegate's approach is being copied. Five schools in the same area have introduced pouches, and Okafor is careful not to claim that the policy has solved every problem. \"Students still have their phones the moment they walk out of the gate, and a lot of what happens online happens in the evening,\" she says. \"What we can do is give them seven hours a day when they have to talk to the person sitting next to them.\""}],"groups":[{"text":0,"instruction":"Questions 28-30. Complete the summary below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the text for each answer.","qtype":"summary","summaryTitle":"How the policy began","questions":[{"n":28,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Within a week of the announcement, more than 500 parents had signed a ___ against the plan.","accept":["petition"],"limit":1,"evidence":"more than 500 parents had signed an online petition against the plan","why":{"en":"\"Signed an online petition against the plan\". ONE WORD ONLY, so write \"petition\", not \"online petition\".","tr":"\"500’den fazla veli plana karşı çevrimiçi bir imza kampanyasını imzalamıştı\". YALNIZCA BİR KELİME: \"online petition\" değil, \"petition\" yaz.","fa":"«یک طومار اینترنتی علیه این طرح امضا کرده بودند». فقط یک کلمه، پس «⁨petition⁩» بنویس، نه «⁨online petition⁩»."},"trap":["TR-limit"]},{"n":29,"kind":"gap","prompt":"The school paid for the pouches out of its own ___.","accept":["budget"],"limit":1,"evidence":"the school paid for them out of its own budget","why":{"en":"\"The school paid for them out of its own budget rather than asking families to contribute\".","tr":"\"Okul, ailelerden katkı istemek yerine bunları kendi bütçesinden ödedi\".","fa":"«مدرسه به‌جای اینکه از خانواده‌ها پول بخواهد، هزینه‌ی کیسه‌ها را از بودجه‌ی خودش داد»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":30,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Before this, the rule about phones had been almost impossible to ___.","accept":["enforce"],"limit":1,"evidence":"a rule that teachers found almost impossible to enforce","why":{"en":"The old rule was one \"that teachers found almost impossible to enforce\". The gap needs a verb.","tr":"Eski kural \"öğretmenlerin uygulatmayı neredeyse imkânsız bulduğu\" bir kuraldı. Boşluk bir fiil ister.","fa":"قانون قبلی «قانونی بود که معلم‌ها اجرا کردنش را تقریباً غیرممکن می‌دانستند». جای خالی یک فعل می‌خواهد."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]}]},{"text":0,"instruction":"Questions 31-36. Look at the following statements (Questions 31-36) and the list of people below. Match each statement with the correct person, A-G. Write the correct letter, A-G, in boxes 31-36 on your answer sheet. NB You may use any letter more than once.","qtype":"match-features","bank":["A Tom Barrett","B Helen Carver","C Paul Hendry","D Amira Shah","E Mark Lindqvist","F Diane Okafor","G Grace Mensah"],"questions":[{"n":31,"kind":"match","prompt":"The policy created extra work for staff at first.","correct":5,"evidence":"staff spent more time dealing with students who refused to hand in their phones","why":{"en":"Okafor: for a few weeks \"staff spent more time dealing with students who refused to hand in their phones\".","tr":"Okafor: Birkaç hafta boyunca \"personel, telefonunu teslim etmeyen öğrencilerle her zamankinden fazla uğraştı\".","fa":"اوکافور: چند هفته «کارکنان بیشتر از همیشه وقت صرف دانش‌آموزهایی کردند که گوشی‌شان را تحویل نمی‌دادند»."},"trap":["TR-whosevoice","TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":32,"kind":"match","prompt":"Students talk to each other more at lunchtime than before.","correct":3,"evidence":"People actually play games and talk to each other","why":{"en":"Shah: lunch is \"louder now, in a good way. People actually play games and talk to each other\".","tr":"Shah: Öğle arası \"artık daha gürültülü, iyi anlamda. İnsanlar gerçekten oyun oynuyor ve birbirleriyle konuşuyor\".","fa":"شاه: وقت ناهار «حالا شلوغ‌تر است، به معنای خوبش. بچه‌ها واقعاً بازی می‌کنند و با هم حرف می‌زنند»."},"trap":["TR-whosevoice","TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":33,"kind":"match","prompt":"Better information would have reduced opposition to the plan.","correct":4,"evidence":"I wish the school had explained that more clearly at the start","why":{"en":"Lindqvist: \"a lot of the anger came from people who didn't understand how it would work\". Hendry only says meetings were held.","tr":"Lindqvist: \"Öfkenin çoğu bunun nasıl işleyeceğini anlamayan insanlardan geldi\". Hendry yalnızca toplantılar yapıldığını söylüyor.","fa":"لیندکوویست: «بیشتر عصبانیت از کسانی بود که نفهمیده بودند این طرح چطور اجرا می‌شود». هِندری فقط می‌گوید جلسه برگزار شده بود."},"trap":["TR-whosevoice","TR-samewords"]},{"n":34,"kind":"match","prompt":"Boredom can lead students to discover a new interest.","correct":0,"evidence":"Then they discover that they actually enjoy it","why":{"en":"Barrett: some come \"because they're bored\", then \"discover that they actually enjoy it\".","tr":"Barrett: Bazıları \"sıkıldıkları için\" geliyor, sonra \"aslında bundan keyif aldıklarını keşfediyorlar\".","fa":"بارت: بعضی‌ها «چون حوصله‌شان سر رفته» می‌آیند و بعد «می‌فهمند که واقعاً از آن لذت می‌برند»."},"trap":["TR-whosevoice","TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":35,"kind":"match","prompt":"It is difficult to know what has caused the improvements.","correct":1,"evidence":"it is very hard to say what has made the difference","why":{"en":"Carver: \"it is very hard to say what has made the difference\".","tr":"Carver: \"Farkı neyin yarattığını söylemek çok zor\".","fa":"کارور: «خیلی سخت است بگوییم چه چیزی این تفاوت را ایجاد کرده»."},"trap":["TR-whosevoice","TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":36,"kind":"match","prompt":"More students use an indoor space when it rains.","correct":6,"evidence":"On wet days, the library is now completely full","why":{"en":"Mensah: \"On wet days, the library is now completely full\": when it rains = on wet days.","tr":"Mensah: \"Yağmurlu günlerde kütüphane artık tamamen dolu\": when it rains = on wet days.","fa":"منسا: «روزهای بارانی کتابخانه حالا کاملاً پر است»: ⁨when it rains⁩ یعنی ⁨on wet days⁩."},"trap":["TR-whosevoice","TR-paraphrase"]}]},{"text":0,"instruction":"Questions 37-40. Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.","qtype":"mcq","questions":[{"n":37,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"Why did the head teacher introduce the policy?","options":["A to help students concentrate in lessons","B to reduce problems outside lessons","C because many parents had asked for it","D to save the school money"],"correct":1,"evidence":"Most of our problems with phones happened at break and lunchtime","why":{"en":"Okafor says it \"was not mainly about lessons\": the problems happened \"at break and lunchtime\".","tr":"Okafor kararın \"esas olarak derslerle ilgili olmadığını\" söylüyor: Sorunlar \"teneffüste ve öğle arasında\" yaşanıyordu.","fa":"اوکافور می‌گوید تصمیم «بیشتر به کلاس‌ها ربطی نداشت»: مشکل‌ها «در زنگ تفریح و وقت ناهار» پیش می‌آمد."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase","TR-samewords"]},{"n":38,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"What do some older students say about the policy?","options":["A It stops them keeping in touch with employers and family.","B It treats them like young children.","C It has made lunchtimes too noisy.","D It does not let them use the office phones."],"correct":0,"evidence":"they can no longer reply to messages about part-time jobs or contact their families during the day","why":{"en":"Older students \"can no longer reply to messages about part-time jobs or contact their families\". B was Amira Shah's first reaction, not theirs.","tr":"Büyük öğrenciler \"yarı zamanlı işlerle ilgili mesajlara artık cevap veremiyor ya da gün içinde aileleriyle iletişim kuramıyor\". B onların değil, Amira Shah’ın ilk tepkisiydi.","fa":"دانش‌آموزهای بزرگ‌تر «دیگر نمی‌توانند به پیام‌های مربوط به کار پاره‌وقتشان جواب بدهند یا در طول روز با خانواده تماس بگیرند». گزینه‌ی ⁨B⁩ واکنش اول امیرا شاه بود، نه آن‌ها."},"trap":["TR-whosevoice","TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":39,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"What does Dr Carver recommend?","options":["A that every school should ban phones","B that exam results should be checked every year","C a long-term study comparing different schools","D asking students for their opinions"],"correct":2,"evidence":"a large study that follows schools with and without bans over several years","why":{"en":"She would like \"a large study that follows schools with and without bans over several years\".","tr":"\"Yasak olan ve olmayan okulları birkaç yıl boyunca izleyen büyük bir araştırma\" görmek istiyor.","fa":"او دلش می‌خواهد «پژوهشی بزرگ ببیند که مدرسه‌های با ممنوعیت و بدون ممنوعیت را چند سال دنبال کند»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":40,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"What is the writer's main purpose in the article?","options":["A to persuade other schools to ban phones","B to explain how phone pouches work","C to criticise parents who opposed the plan","D to report one school's experience and different views of it"],"correct":3,"evidence":"Students' views are mixed","why":{"en":"The article describes the policy and gives the views of students, parents, staff and a researcher without taking a side. B covers only one paragraph.","tr":"Makale politikayı anlatıyor ve taraf tutmadan öğrencilerin, velilerin, personelin ve bir araştırmacının görüşlerini veriyor. B yalnızca bir paragrafı kapsıyor.","fa":"مقاله این سیاست را توصیف می‌کند و بدون طرف‌داری، نظر دانش‌آموزها، والدین، کارکنان و یک پژوهشگر را می‌آورد. گزینه‌ی ⁨B⁩ فقط یک پاراگراف را پوشش می‌دهد."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]}]}],"id":"c-x11-r3-d-gt","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-11","unit":"x11-r3"},"exit":{"type":"exit","items":[{"tests":"word","point":1,"prompt":"\"A rule that teachers found almost impossible to enforce.\" To enforce a rule is to...","options":["make people obey it","write it down","change it"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"Enforce = make sure people follow a rule.","tr":"Enforce = insanların bir kurala uymasını sağlamak.","fa":"⁨enforce⁩ یعنی کاری کنی که مردم قانون را رعایت کنند."}},{"tests":"paraphrase","point":1,"prompt":"A statement says \"when it rains\". Which words in an article mean the same?","options":["on wet days","at lunchtime","in the first term"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"Wet days = days when it rains.","tr":"Wet days = yağmurlu günler.","fa":"⁨wet days⁩ یعنی روزهای بارانی."}},{"tests":"method","point":2,"prompt":"A summary says ONE WORD ONLY, and the text says \"an online petition\". What do you write?","options":["online petition","petition","an online petition"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"One word only: \"petition\". The other answers have two and three words.","tr":"Yalnızca bir kelime: \"petition\". Diğer cevaplar iki ve üç kelime.","fa":"فقط یک کلمه: «⁨petition⁩». جواب‌های دیگر دو و سه کلمه‌اند."}},{"tests":"trap","point":3,"prompt":"\"Amira Shah says lunch is louder now. Some older students complain that they cannot contact their families.\" Who says students cannot contact their families?","options":["Amira Shah","a group of students, not a named person","the writer, as a personal opinion"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"The complaint is reported for a group of older students; it is neither Shah's quote nor the writer's own view.","tr":"Şikâyet bir grup büyük öğrenciye ait olarak aktarılıyor; ne Shah’ın sözü ne de yazarın kendi görüşü.","fa":"این شکایت از زبان گروهی از دانش‌آموزهای بزرگ‌تر نقل شده؛ نه حرف شاه است و نه نظر خود نویسنده."}}],"id":"c-x11-r3-x-gt","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-11","unit":"x11-r3"}}}; })(globalThis.IELTS_EXAMS = globalThis.IELTS_EXAMS || {});
